RFC 7529 RSCALE examples

Source: RFC 7529, "Non-Gregorian Recurrence Rules in the Internet Calendaring and
Scheduling Core Object Specification (iCalendar)", C. Daboo and
G. Yakushev, May 2015, section 4.3.
URL: https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7529#section-4.3

cases.json contains the DTSTART and RRULE lines of the examples in
section 4.3 and the Gregorian instances from the example tables. Changes:
- The non-Gregorian examples keep the RFC instances in "notes" and expect an
  "unsupported calendar scale" error.
- The Gregorian leap day example without RSCALE adds 20200229 from the prose.
tools/extract_rfc7529.py makes the file. RFC 7529 has no errata.

